WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.510
Hello, I'm Gav.

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:02.343
I'm Dan.

00:00:02.343 --> 00:00:03.370
We're the Slow Mo Guys.

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:05.453
Dan, do you know what else
is a bloody good channel

00:00:05.453 --> 00:00:06.286
for YouTube?
Go on.

00:00:06.286 --> 00:00:07.500
The hydraulic press channel.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:08.350
Yeah, it's pretty sweet.

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:09.710
We've got one here.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:10.620
It is massive.
Yeah.

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:11.453
Look at the size of the thing.

00:00:11.453 --> 00:00:14.980
It actually goes about probably
12, 15 feet up in the air.

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:16.160
It's huge.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:17.480
And I've learnt from that channel,

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:19.180
that pretty much anything explodes

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:20.540
if you press on it hard enough.

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:22.280
Including, a deck of cards,

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:24.000
which I just happen to have in my car.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.990
I know, we've never seen, I've never seen

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:28.500
the hydraulic press blow
something up in slow motion.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:29.333
No.

00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:32.920
So we're gonna film this
at 28,500 frames a second,

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.610
which is over a thousand
times slower than you can see

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:37.510
with your own face.

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:39.410
So on the hydraulic press channel,

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:41.270
the cards explode basically.

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:42.903
So to protect us and the camera,

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:45.980
we've had to put this thick
screen in front of us.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:47.270
Because I don't really particularly want

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:49.797
a piece of card going through
my jugular as we're filming.

00:00:49.797 --> 00:00:51.011
Kill buddy is suspended.

00:00:51.011 --> 00:00:54.370
Yeah, so if it does explode,

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:56.750
I wanna be protected, instead of...

00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:57.860
Thankfully this hydraulic press,

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:00.130
you can see all the way
through to the other side.

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:01.610
'Cause typically it's quite hard to light

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:02.740
inside machinery like that.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:05.830
And we also got ourselves a
lovely, bright light here,

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:08.430
that I'm blasting down in
the face of Dan right now.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:11.660
So we should get some
nice exposure on this.

00:01:14.006 --> 00:01:15.423
And we have 25,

00:01:17.857 --> 00:01:19.492
30, 40,

00:01:19.492 --> 00:01:20.325
50,

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:22.423
60, 70,

00:01:26.344 --> 00:01:27.177
80,

00:01:29.142 --> 00:01:29.975
90.

00:01:32.286 --> 00:01:33.119
Oh God.

00:01:36.088 --> 00:01:37.010
Flip.

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:38.510
Oh my God.

00:02:09.687 --> 00:02:13.060
Well this is all we got
left, it's this and this.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:15.830
So this is actually all 52 cards

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:18.160
compressed as much as possible.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:21.590
So technically this is a full
deck of cards right here.

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:23.110
Every single card in the deck is squashed.

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:26.150
Sort of like crushes it back to wood.

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:28.250
It does, it's pretty solid,
I wonder if it will snap.

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:29.529
I thought we were gonna die.

00:02:29.529 --> 00:02:31.970
Yeah, glad we had that cover,

00:02:31.970 --> 00:02:33.840
because all the cards
flung out everywhere,

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:34.680
all over the floor.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:35.550
Well I thought that was a lovely

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:37.730
little tribute video there.

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:38.860
Nice, quick, easy one.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:39.700
Pick a card, any card.

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:40.533
Okay.

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:43.440
Well you've got the
jack of diamonds there.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:44.273
Yeah.

00:02:44.273 --> 00:02:45.360
Yeah, you weren't supposed
to show me, but...

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:46.260
Oh, sorry, yeah.

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:51.060
Well, all you have to do is
say, "Is this your card?"

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:52.140
And the answer is yes.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:53.660
'Cause it's definitely...
Its every card

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:54.493
Yeah.

00:02:54.493 --> 00:02:56.212
All right, well, feel free
to follow us on Twitter.

00:02:56.212 --> 00:02:59.240
We've got so much, we've
got a lovely second channel.

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:00.710
And do let us know in the comments,

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:04.930
if you'd like to see any
more slow-mo hydraulic press.

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:07.260
I'm sure we can make that one happen.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:09.090
This is the only one that's intact.

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:10.547
All right, we'll see you in the next one.

